    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0492" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg206"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2508</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-16T19:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1916, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 18, 8.15 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3635. Great prominence given by German press to reports of trouble with Mexico.
                    Several papers think the Japanese are mixed up in the matter and are secretly
                    backing Villa. Resignation of Von
                        Tirpitz now publicly confirmed and Von Capelle named as probable successor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
